# Build-context exclusions for the three builder images.
#
# None of Dockerfile-build, Dockerfile-build-linux-arm64 or
# Dockerfile-build-linux-x86_64 carries a COPY or ADD today: they install a
# toolchain and run maturin against a bind-mounted /io, so nothing from this
# context currently reaches a layer. This file is the guard for the day one of
# them grows a COPY, because `docker build` still uploads the whole context to
# the daemon and a COPY . added later would pull in every path listed below.
#
# Patterns are written in BOTH root-anchored and **/-anchored forms on purpose:
# a bare "*.pem" matches only the context root, so key material one directory
# down (which is exactly where docker/server.pem lives) would still be shipped.

# --- Key material ---------------------------------------------------------
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
id_rsa
**/id_rsa
id_ed25519
**/id_ed25519
*.keystore
**/*.keystore
.netrc
**/.netrc
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.pypirc
**/.pypirc

# --- Credential-carrying config -------------------------------------------
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
*.tfvars
**/*.tfvars
.aws/
**/.aws/
.docker/config.json
**/.docker/config.json

# The local ArangoDB test fixture: TLS material plus the JWT files
# docker/start_db.sh generates at run time.
docker/server.pem
docker/jwtHeader
docker/jwtSecret

# --- Build and VCS noise, so the context stays small ----------------------
.git/
.github/
target/
dist/
build/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
